Inbound SimpleX images and documents never reached the agent.

An attachment's newChatItems event arrives BEFORE the file downloads,
so chatItem.file.fileSource.filePath is absent. The adapter deferred
only audio at that point; every other kind fell through:

1. The chat item was delivered immediately, without the file (the
   media_urls block at the bottom of _handle_chat_item is inside
   `if file_path:`).
2. Nothing parked the item in _pending_file_transfers, so when the
   download did complete (rcvFileDescrReady -> /freceive ->
   rcvFileComplete), the completion handler found no pending entry and
   dropped the file for good.

Observed live: a picture sent from the phone produced a text-only
message on the agent's side and nothing else.

The rcvFileComplete path is generic already - it re-injects filePath
and re-handles the item - so the fix is only to widen the defer guard
from audio to any not-yet-downloaded file that has a fileId. A missing
fileId cannot be addressed by /freceive and still falls through.

Same tradeoff audio already accepted: if /freceive fails (expired
transfer), the deferred item is never delivered. The double /freceive
that rcvFileDescrReady may also send is harmless - the daemon answers
the second one with an error, and the send is fire-and-forget.

Still present in upstream v2026.9.14: the guard reads
`not file_path and _is_audio_ext(ext)`.

--- a/platforms/simplex/adapter.py
+++ b/platforms/simplex/adapter.py
@@ -368,10 +368,12 @@
             ext = Path(file_path).suffix.lower() if file_path else ""
             if not ext and file_info.get("fileName", ""):
                 ext = Path(file_info["fileName"]).suffix.lower()
-            # Voice notes typically arrive before the file finishes downloading; defer until
-            # rcvFileComplete. /freceive gets no corrId reply, so awaiting one would block the loop.
-            if not file_path and _is_audio_ext(ext) and file_id is not None:
-                logger.info("SimpleX: voice file %d not yet received, accepting transfer", file_id)
+            # Attachments arrive before the file finishes downloading; defer until
+            # rcvFileComplete. Delivering now would strip the file, and the completion
+            # handler only re-delivers items parked here. /freceive gets no corrId
+            # reply, so awaiting one would block the loop.
+            if not file_path and file_id is not None:
+                logger.info("SimpleX: file %d not yet received, accepting transfer", file_id)
                 self._pending_file_transfers[file_id] = chat_item
                 await self._send_fire_and_forget(f"/freceive {file_id}")
                 return
